  "term": "perceptual anchoring",
  "definition": "Perceptual anchoring is the ability to use repeated presentations of the same or similar stimuli to improve perceptual performance. In this source, it refers to benefiting from stimulus repetition rather than having difficulty filtering out external visual noise.",
